        Hi my name is Mike Farrell and I am 19 years old. I am living in 
Severna Park, MD USA.I really find it boring around here and I've looked 
into both of the local LUG's in my area (annapolis and glen burnie).  
Neither one really seems to be 100% organized or consistent at the moment.  

        I'm interested in founding a weekly or monthly Severna Park Linux 
User Group for all of us around here that are tired of sitting in our 
houses and doing nothing on Monday nights.  

        As of right now this is merely a proposal and I won't go through 
with this if I don't get at least 2 emails of interest.  I am very open to 
suggestions right now as for meeting points and schedules.  I can also say 
that anyone that joins this group will get their time's worth.  Since I 
started using this OS i have been able to do the following independent of 
windows:

        *Compile and install a recent kernel fine tuned to my system.
        *Get my partitioned usb hard drive to work in linux
        *Run a working personal HTTP /w PHP and FTP server.
        *Download/play mp3's and Burn CD's using command line cdrecord 
utility.
        *Develop free video games for the Linux OS.
        *Watch decent framerated DVD'S with menu support now thanks to OGLE.
        *Run remote terminal & X sessions between my laptop back and forth 
and share files through samba.

I'd be willing to show other people how to do all this stuff themselves :-).

I'll also be hosting the web page for the LUG if it takes off on a  
subdirectory of my web site:
http://ltsword.allegronetwork.com

If anyone in the area is interested in starting up this group, please email 
me at gccdragoonkain@yahoo.com.

Thanks

